{
 "why": "WHAT THE BYTES ACTUALLY SAY. An .m4a carries no record of the words it was rendered from, so once the manifest is regenerated there is nothing left to compare a paid clip against -- the manifest would simply claim the new, correct title while the file on disk still speaks the old one. That is not hypothetical: three clips here were rendered from a mis-paired title and say a different song's name, and nothing caught it because no check compared a clip to anything. This file is that missing record. render-titles.py writes an entry the moment it produces bytes, and check-title-clips.mjs fails when an entry disagrees with the manifest without an awaitingRerender note explaining why.",
 "writtenBy": "music-book/tools/render-titles.py, checked by music-book/tools/check-title-clips.mjs",
 "seededOn": "2026-09-22",
 "seededFrom": "audio/titles/manifest.json as it stood at commit bf97f89f, which is the only surviving record of the text the 54 existing clips were rendered from.",
